# /join/<code> is one page: join.html reads the code from the address.
# A 200 rule rewrites without changing the URL. The code is never sent anywhere.
# The target is /join, not /join.html: Pages redirects *.html to the
# extension-less path (308), which would drop the code from the address
# (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/serving-pages/, read 2026-11-05).
/join/*  /join  200
